<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένος</span></b> , 
			Lacon.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρσένος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Lys.</u>
			1263
		</span></i> (lyr.). ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>maiden, girl</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.127
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἄθλιαι π.
			ἐμαί</span> my unhappy <i>girls</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1462
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1302
			</span></i> ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνὴ παρθένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					514
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. κόρα</span>, of the Sphinx,
			dub. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1730
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγάτηρ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.6.9
			</span></i> ; of Persephone, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1342
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				804
			</span></i>; <i>virgin</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυνή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				148
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				27.65
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of unmarried
			women who are not virgins, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.514
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				3.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1219
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				530
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παρθένος, ἡ</span>, <i>the Virgin Goddess</i>, as a title of
			Athena at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				5.11.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.34.8
			</span></i> (hence of an 
				Att.
			 coin bearing her head, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				675
			</span></i>); of Artemis, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				17
			</span></i> ; of the Tauric Iphigenia, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.103
			</span></i> ; of an unnamed goddess, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				46.3
			</span></i> (Halic., <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.108.48
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				54
			</span></i> (Neapolis in Thrace); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἱεραὶ
			π</span>., of the Vestal Virgins, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.69
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.89e
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ Ἑστιάδες π</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				19
			</span></i>; simply, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.66
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> the
			constellation <u>Virgo</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Eudox.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				1.2.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				97
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>, <i>pupil</i>, X.ap.Longin.<i><span class="en">
				4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <i>maiden, chaste</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένον ψυχὴν ἔχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					1006
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				33
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίτρη π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				319
			</span></i> : metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πηγή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					613
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> as masc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένος, ὁ</span>, <i>unmarried man,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Apoc.
				14.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. γῆ</span>
			<i>Samian earth</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Berol.</u>
				2.57
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
